# 307: line tracking THROUGH a multi-line string literal. The literal spans lines
# 1-3, so the two newlines inside it must advance the line counter: the failing
# `1 / 0` is on line 5, and a lexer that did not count them would report 3.
# len() is bytes, so "one\ntwo\nthree" is 13.
--- source
let s = "one
two
three";
print len(s);
print 1 / 0;
--- expect
13
error: Value at line 5: divide by zero
